## DTO Shapes (current, verified against source — not framework class names, plain dicts/interfaces)

### Simulate Request (FE → BE)
`QMCB-fe/src/interfaces/unitary.ts` → `UnitaryRequestDTO`:
```typescript
{
  target_unitary: Gate;
  number_of_qubits: number;
  gates: UnitaryGateEntry[];        // string | { gate, theta?, alpha?, beta?, gamma? }
  qubit_order: AnyQubitOrder[];
  seed?: number;
  target_params?: TargetParamsDTO;  // { seed?, alpha?, beta?, gamma?, delta?, theta? }
  parameter_gate_index?: number;
}
```
Parameterized gates (theta on Rx/Ry/Rz trial steps) are fully implemented end-to-end.

**Known open gap:** `target_params.theta` is defined on both FE and BE DTOs but
`QMCB-be/app/utils/unitary_payload.py`'s parser never reads `theta` from `target_params`, and
never unwraps a nested `target_params` object at all — only reads `seed`/`alpha`/`beta`/
`gamma`/`delta` from the request root. FE-built `target_params.theta` is currently dead on
arrival; the resolver falls back to extracting theta from the trial circuit instead. This
hasn't caused visible bugs (the fallback works) but is real tech debt if `target_params.theta`
is ever relied on directly.

### Simulate Response (BE → FE)
Built as a plain dict in `controllers/simulate.py` (no DTO class):
```python
{
    "message": str,
    "grading_mode": "random_theta" | "unitary_global_phase" | None,
    "samples_checked": int | None,
    "samples_passed": int | None,
    "trial_truth_table": dict | None,
    "target_truth_table": dict | None,
    "all_match": bool,
    "validation_mode": bool,
}
```
`validation_mode` — confirmed **fixed**, no trailing colon. (This was a Week-1-era bug; do not
reintroduce it.)

