## Starting Primitives (gates available from game start)

Students begin each session with: **Rz(θ)** and **√X** (SQRT_X).
Note: earlier project docs said "Rx(π/2)" here — that was imprecise. The actual starting gate
is √X, a fixed non-parameterized gate. It's matrix-equivalent to Rx(π/2) up to global phase, but
it is not the parameterized Rx gate — don't conflate the two when working on starting-gate logic.

